## Original Content
Chinese President Xi Jinping on Monday afternoon held a welcome ceremony for King of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein, who is on a state visit to China, at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing.

## Summary
Chinese President Xi Jinping hosted a welcome ceremony for King Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein of Jordan at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing on Monday afternoon. The ceremony was part of the Jordanian king's state visit to China.

## Key Points
- Xi Jinping held a welcome ceremony for King Abdullah II ibn Al Hussein during his state visit to China.
- The ceremony took place at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing.
- The event occurred on Monday afternoon, highlighting diplomatic relations between China and Jordan.


